#: ../userguides/forest_chm_benchmark_2026-08-31.rst:9
#: 6ad73cccf59440849dfedceca125e8aa
msgid "🌲 Canopy Height Model (CHM) — per-location benchmark (v.2026-08-31)"
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/forest_chm_benchmark_2026-08-31.rst:11
#: 1de578d28ad0498eab8bf2308e1f6997
msgid "This page details the **Canopy Height Model (CHM)** produced by the 🌲 Forest and trees **Height estimation** option. **CHM v.2026-08-31** is compared against **CHM v.2026-07-03** on the most-improved sample per country, using lidar-derived ground truth aggregated to 5 m hexagons (max height)."
msgstr ""

#: ../userguides/forest_chm_benchmark_2026-08-31.rst:15
#: 719d3da77810427888ce1e79694f0e13
msgid "The metric is the **mean absolute error (MAE)** of canopy height, in metres, against the lidar ground truth. Across 38 areas of interest, CHM v.2026-08-31 lowers the mean MAE from **4.70 m to 3.24 m (−31%)** versus CHM v.2026-07-03, with the largest gains in tall, structurally complex forest."
msgstr ""

